time window (Tables 1\u20133), movie properties (name, rating, closed captions), park properties (name, phone, zip, community, park URL, and a free-text location/address that often embeds coordinates), optional contact person/email (Tables 2\u20133), and optional sponsorship/underwriter (Tables 4\u20136). To keep the integrated schema minimal in table count while still complete, a single entity type EventScreening is used that can represent every row across all sources; columns not present in a given source stay NULL. Attribute names are normalized (e.g., Rating -> movie_rating; Location/Location 1 -> park_address_text). Latitude/longitude are included as separate attributes to represent coordinates that appear in the location text in some tables; they can be parsed when available without adding redundant raw coordinate columns. Park-related fields are kept with a park_* prefix to preserve semantics even though they are stored on the EventScreening entity."}, "time": 15.99201410007663}, "1": {"response": {"integrated_schemas": {"EventScreening": {"integrated_schema": ["event_name", "event_url", "start_datetime", "end_datetime", "movie_name", "movie_rating", "movie_closed_caption", "park_name", "park_url", "park_phone", "park_zip_code", "community_area", "park_location_text", "park_location_1_text", "latitude", "longitude", "underwriter_name", "contact_name", "contact_email"]}}, "input_column_mappings": {"Table 1": {"EventName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "event_name"}, "MovieName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_name"}, "ParkName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_name"}, "ZipCode": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_zip_code"}, "Phone": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_phone"}, "StartDate": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "start_datetime"}, "End