bute": "movie_rating"}, "Location 1": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_location_1_text"}}, "Table 3": {"EventName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "event_name"}, "MovieName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_name"}, "MovieClosedCaption": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_closed_caption"}, "MovieRating": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_rating"}, "Location": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_name"}, "Zipcode": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_zip_code"}, "Phone": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_phone"}, "ContactName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "contact_name"}, "ContactEmail": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "contact_email"}, "Location 1": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_location_1_text"}}, "Table 4": {"ParkName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_name"}, "Phone": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_phone"}, "MovieName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_name"}, "MovieRating": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_rating"}, "Underwriter": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "underwriter_name"}, "Location": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_location_text"}}, "Table 5": {"ParkName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_name"}, "Phone": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_phone"}, "MovieName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_name"}, "MovieRating": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_rating"}, "Underwriter": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "underwriter_name"}, "Location": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_location_text"}}, "Table 6": {"ParkName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_name"}, "Phone": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_phone"}, "MovieName": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_name"}, "Rating": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "movie_rating"}, "Underwriter": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "underwriter_name"}, "Location": {"entity_type": "EventScreening", "integrated_schema_attribute": "park_location_text"}}}, "reasoning": "All six sources describe outdoor movie showings that occur at specific parks/venues, sometimes with explicit event-level data (event name, URL, start/end datetime) and sometimes only a park+movie program row (with underwriter). To keep the integrated schema minimal in number of tables while still complete, a single entity type EventScreening is used to represent one screening/program row, with optional attributes populated depending on source availability. Attributes were unified by meaning and naming: MovieRating/Rating -> movie_rating; ZipCode/Zipcode -> park_zip_code; Location (table 4-6) and Location 1 (tables 1-3) are kept as separate raw text fields because they carry different formats and preserving both avoids information loss. Latitude/longitude are included for semantic correctness because several Location fields embed coordinates; these can be parsed into the dedicated attributes while retaining the original strings. Park-related fields (name/url/phone/zip/community/location) are included on the screening entity to avoid introducing additional tables/joins while still covering all source attributes; duplicates across rows are expected but do not add new attributes and keep the schema understandable and compact. Contact and underwriter fields are modeled as optional screening attributes because they are provided per event/program record in the sources."}, "time": 17.787634199950844}, "2": {"response": {"integrated_schemas": {"EventScreening": {"integrated_schema": ["event_name", "event_url", "start_datetime", "end_datetime", "movie_name", "movie_rating", "movie_closed_caption_flag", "park_name", "park_url", "park_phone", "park_zip_code", "community_area", "underwriter_name", "contact_name", "contact_email", "location_address_text", "location_latitude", "location_longitude"]}}, "input_column_mappings": {"Table 1": {"EventName": {"EventScreening": "event_name"}, "MovieName": {"EventScreening": "movie_name"}, "ParkName": {"EventScreening": "park_name"}, "ZipCode": {"EventScreening": "park_zip_code"}, "Phone": {"EventScreening": "park_phone"}, "StartDate": {"EventScreening": "start_datetime"}, "EndDate": {"EventScreening": "end_datetime"}, "EventUrl": {"EventScreening": "event_url"}, "ParkUrl": {"EventScreening": "park_url"}, "Community": {"EventScreening": "community_area"}, "MovieClosedCaption": {"EventScreening": "movie_closed_caption_flag"}, "MovieRating": {"EventScreening": "movie_rating"}, "Location 1": {"EventScreening": "location_address_text"}}, "Table 2": {"EventName": {"EventScreening": "event_name"}, "MovieName": {"EventScreening": "movie_name"}, "ParkName": {"EventScreening": "park_name"}, "ZipCode": {"EventScreening": "park_zip_code"}, "Phone": {"EventScreening": "park_phone"}, "StartDate": {"EventScreening": "start_datetime"}, "EndDate": {"EventScreening": "end_datetime"}, "ContactName": {"EventScreening": "contact_name"}, "ContactEmail": {"EventScreening": "contact_email"}, "EventUrl": {"EventScreening": "event_url"}, "ParkUrl": {"EventScreening": "park_url"}, "Community": {"EventScreening": "community_area"}, "MovieClosedCaption": {"EventScreening": "movie_closed_caption_flag"}, "MovieRating": {"EventScreening": "movie_rating"}, "Location 1": {"EventScreening": "location_address_text"}}, "Table 3": {"EventName": {"EventScreening": "event_name"}, "MovieName": {"EventScreening": "movie_name"}, "MovieClosedCaption": {"EventScreening": "movie_closed_caption_flag"}, "MovieRating": {"EventScreening": "movie_rating"}, "Location": {"EventScreening": "park_name"}, "Zipcode": {"EventScreening": "park_zip_code"}, "Phone": {"EventScreening": "park_phone"}, "ContactName": {"EventScreening": "contact_name"}, "ContactEmail": {"EventScreening": "contact_email"}, "Location 1": {"EventScreening": "location_address_text"}}, "Table 4": {"ParkName": {"EventScreening": "park_name"}, "Phone": {"EventScreening": "park_phone"}, "MovieName": {"EventScreening": "movie_name"}, "MovieRating": {"EventScreening": "movie_rating"}, "Underwriter": {"EventScreening": "underwriter_name"}, "Location": {"EventScreening": "location_address_text"}}, "Table 5": {"ParkName": {"EventScreening": "park_name"}, "Phone": {"EventScreening": "park_phone"}, "MovieName": {"EventScreening": "movie_name"}, "MovieRating": {"EventScreening": "movie_rating"}, "Underwriter": {"EventScreening": "underwriter_name"}, "Location": {"EventScreening": "location_address_text"}}, "Table 6": {"ParkName": {"EventScreening": "park_name"}, "Phone": {"EventScreening": "park_phone"}, "MovieName": {"EventScreening": "movie_name"}, "Rating": {"EventScreening": "movie_rating"}, "Underwriter": {"EventScreening": "underwriter_name"}, "Location": {"EventScreening": "location_address_text"}}}, "reasoning": "Identified one dominant entity type across all sources: a movie screening occurrence tied to a specific park/location, with optional metadata varying by year/program (event URLs, contacts, community, underwriter). To keep the integrated schema minimal and redundancy-free given the lack of stable identifiers for separate Park/Movie/Contact entities and inconsistent attribute availability, all attributes are represented on a single EventScreening entity with nullable optional fields. Column harmonization includes: (1) normalizing ZipCode/Zipcode to park_zip_code, (2) normalizing MovieRating/Rating to movie_rating, (3) mapping Table 3 'Location' (park name) to park_name, (4) capturing various 'Location'/'Location 1' free-text address+lat/long strings in location_address_text while also providing atomic latitude/longitude fields for parsed coordinates when available, and (5) including underwriter and contact fields as optional attributes because they appear only in some tables."}, "time": 12.767826700117439}}